2.1 Problem Statement (A1)

The UAPS ePelekat Kenderaan system interface provides multiple sections of application form, including applicant information, vehicle details, supporting documents and emergency contact information on a continuous page. This requires users to scroll through several sections that make the application process less organized and convenient.
As a result, users may miss certain required fields or leave information incomplete, which could lead to application errors. Besides, the dashboard of the system provides a sidebar menu for accessing through different services such as checking status, sticker cancellation or replacement. 
However, the lack of a clear overview of important information such as current application status, registered vehicle details and recent activities on the dashboard features may require users to navigate into different pages to find information they need quickly, making it less convenient and informative.
Furthermore, the application status interface mainly presents information in a table format without a clear visual representation count of application progress. This may make it difficult for users to understand where exactly their current application stage and identify the next required action. 
Therefore, the improvement aim will be made to provide a more organized, accessible and user-friendly experience for UiTM users.
